  "scope": "Two independent author roots reproduce the complete Maven package. Offline installation follows author removal; Java and Kotlin callers run after moving the installed tree and again from a source-free deployment, giving six executions per selection, and compile-time API and Kotlin nullability probes check the generated surface. The full fixture checks per-site constructor selection and normalization over all nineteen primitive bases, fixed-width wrapping, signed zero, refused non-finite floats, Unicode scalars, binary bytes, active variant branches, aliases, mixed Fin guards, exact rejection paths, host conversion refusals, caller-input preservation and recovery after rejection. Independent controls replay the retained records with coordinated record, execution, probe, package, compiler-model and resource mutations. Primitive-base nominal JVM acceptance covers the tested acyclic records, variants, aliases, nested Pair/Array/Option/Except values, mixed Fin guards and constructor-free results over Unit, Bool, UInt8, UInt16, UInt32, UInt64, Int8, Int16, Int32, Int64, Nat, Int, Float32, Float, String, ByteArray, Char, USize and ISize with JDK 22.0.2 and Kotlin 2.2.0 through offline Maven-package installation on Linux x64/glibc 2.36 with an explicit 2.36 package floor and 64-bit machine words. Java and Kotlin consumers run after relocation and again after removal of all consumer sources. Refined callbacks, owned, recursive, dependent and broader generic Subtypes remain pending. Constructor/source entry counts and memory are unmeasured; local runs do not establish hosted 2.38 release-floor acceptance.",
